# Deployment environments

Canonical reference: `docs/architecture/deployment-environments.md`. Runtime
config: `apps/edubridge/lib/deployment-environment.ts`.

## Environment contract

- Next.js owns `NODE_ENV`. Never set it in `.env.local`, Vercel, or Coolify.
  `pnpm dev` → `development`; deployed `next build` → `production`.
- Product/security gates use `NODE_ENV === "production"`, not branch name.
- `APP_ENV` is for hostname/routing only: `local`, `staging`, `production`.
- Local conveniences (any email, demo accounts, dev HMAC fallbacks) apply when
  `NODE_ENV !== "production"`.

| Deployment | Branch | `APP_ENV` | Workspace root |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Local | feature work | `local` | localhost path / `*.localhost` |
| Vercel staging | `development` | `staging` | `dev.edubridge.app` |
| Coolify production | `main` | `production` | `edubridge.app` |

## Invariants

- Staging runs a production build (`NODE_ENV=production`) with separate
  `APP_ENV`, data, and secrets from Coolify production.
- Never expose demo credentials, seed hints, debug pages, detailed errors, or
  predictable signing secrets when `NODE_ENV=production`.
- Never point staging at production Supabase, service-role keys, databases, or
  integration credentials.
- `PLATFORM_DOMAIN` remains the branded public domain. Deployment routing uses
  `WORKSPACE_ROOT_DOMAIN`; do not create another brand constant.
- Generated `*.vercel.app` URLs stay in path mode. Tenant staging uses
  `*.dev.edubridge.app`.
- Keep cookies host-only; never set `Domain=.edubridge.app` or
  `Domain=.dev.edubridge.app`.
- Trust forwarded host headers only behind the configured Vercel/Traefik proxy.
  Do not publish the application container port directly.
- Vercel deploys `development` through Git integration. Coolify production
  consumes a prebuilt image from `main`; builds must not run on the VPS.
- Database migrations are an explicit approved release step, never part of
  build, CI, application boot, or Vercel deployment.
